      "the_1457_mainz_psalter_fust_sch_ffer_u": "The 1457 Mainz Psalter (Fust & Schöffer) used a complicated two-color printing technique: the body type in black, the large initial capitals printed in red and blue on the same impression. This required printing each page through the press in multiple passes with the type inked in different colors. Most scholars consider it among the most beautifully printed books ever made.",
