      "hallmark_american_greetings_papyrus_th": "Hallmark, American Greetings, Papyrus. The greeting card industry + the ephemera-collecting tradition.",
      "hand_bookbinding_often_called_fine_bin": "Hand bookbinding (often called \"fine binding\") never died. Practitioners working in the 1500-style sewn-board-leather tradition exist today at conservation labs (Library of Congress, British Library), at private artisan studios, and in book arts programs (North Bennet Street School in Boston, the Center for Book Arts in New York, Penland in North Carolina). A high-end hand binding still takes weeks + costs $300-$3,000 per book. Industrial case-bound + perfect-bound books are produced by the million on automated lines for $0.50-$3 each. Both descend from the medieval codex.",
      "hand_coloring_1450_chromolithography_1": "Hand-coloring (1450-) → chromolithography (1837-) → photogravure (1880s) → CMYK offset (1950s) → digital RGB. How color got into print.",
